{"approved_definition": "Safety, harmony, and stability of society, of relationships, and of self. Derives from basic individual and group requirements for survival and welfare (cf. Kluckhohn, 1951; Maslow, 1965). Some security values serve primarily individual interests (e.g., health), others wider group interests (e.g., national security).", "core_value": "security", "sources": [{"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:6", "journal_entry": "Picked up the motorcycle from Raul this morning. It rides clean now, brakes feel solid. That's something. But I'm running on maybe four hours of sleep from the last few days and I can feel it in my eyes, in the way I'm slow to react at intersections. Almost clipped a bus mirror on Corrientes.

Saturday is coming and Cacho already texted about the parrilla. Part of me wants to skip it this week, save the money. But another part of me — the louder part — says that's the one thing that keeps me sane. You take away the asado with friends and what do I have left? A cat, a calculator, and a leaking faucet in my own bathroom that I haven't even bothered to fix.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:8", "journal_entry": "Graciela came over unannounced today while I was between deliveries. She brought empanadas, which was nice, except then she sat at my kitchen table and started doing that thing she does where she looks around the apartment cataloguing everything that's wrong. The peeling paint above the window, the chair with the broken leg, the fact that I still don't have a proper desk and eat on the couch.

Then she said — and I quote — "Roberto, you're almost fifty, you can't live like a college student." And I just stood there holding an empanada feeling like I was fourteen again getting lectured. She doesn't see that I actually like my life most of the time. I like picking my own hours. I like riding through Palermo on a Tuesday morning with the sun out and nobody telling me where to be. But she looks at this apartment and she sees failure. And the worst part is that sometimes, when she leaves, I start seeing it through her eyes too.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:5", "journal_entry": "Couldn't sleep. Opened the app at 1am to see if there were any late-night delivery runs. There were two. I took them both, rode the bicycle I borrowed from my neighbor. Came home at 3am with barely enough to cover tomorrow's gas.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Feeling calm and secure in my life"}
